+    carries a ``children`` edge (``split.py:392-395``, written by ``split.accept``,
+    ``split.py:635``). Naming the children is the only safe recovery: ``rm -rf`` on a
+    split parent would destroy the lineage record that is the one place the split's
+    edges live on disk (``split.py:39-42``), orphaning the children it already produced
+    (issue #468's concrete defect — the single-id short circuit used to print exactly
+    that ``rm -rf`` hint for a terminal split parent)."""
+    record = split.read_lineage(d)
+    children = record.get("children") if record else None
+    if not children:
+        return ""
+    return f" — split into children; drive them instead: pdca flow {' '.join(children)}"
+
